OL,3,GNEWSAI'm leaving the BBC after MS pain
OL,4,Amade it hard to carry on
OL,5,
OL,6,FI have lived and worked with multiple
OL,7,Fsclerosis for 26 years, almost as long
OL,8,Fas I have been a BBC Scotland
OL,9,Fjournalist, but recently I have been
OL,10,Fabsent from the airwaves.
OL,12,FI've been struggling with a condition
OL,13,Fcalled trigeminal neuralgia that causes
OL,14,Fexcruciating pain like an electric
OL,15,Fshock across the side of my face, which
OL,16,Fcan stop me from speaking, eating or
OL,17,Fdrinking.
OL,19,FIt's not part of everyone's life with
OL,20,FMS but it has recently become part of
OL,21,Fmine - and being unable to speak is not
OL,22,Fgreat for a broadcaster.
OL,23,APub: 28-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,426,420,260,160,0,100
